== Summary of modifications ==

This directory (`skills/agent-harness/` and `skills/agent-harness-evolve/`)
is a derivative work that rewrites the original content to be
agentic-tool-agnostic, for use with the `npx skills add`-style
Agent Skills convention instead of exclusively with Claude Code. In
particular:

- Replaced every reference to Claude Code's proprietary multi-agent
  APIs (the `Workflow` tool and its `agent()`/`pipeline()`/`parallel()`/
  `phase()` script primitives, `Agent(name:)` + `SendMessage` +
  `TaskCreate`/`TaskUpdate`/`TaskList`/`TaskGet`/`TaskStop`,
  `TeamCreate`/`TeamDelete`, and the `CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS`
  flag) with three portable execution primitives described in
  vendor-neutral terms: checklist-driven delegation, file-mediated
  coordination, and one-shot delegation.
- Replaced fixed Claude Code paths (`.claude/agents/`, `.claude/skills/`,
  `CLAUDE.md`) with guidance to use whatever agent/skill convention the
  host project already has, defaulting to `AGENTS/` and `skills/`.
- Renamed the Claude-specific model tiers `fable`/`opus`/`sonnet` to the
  vendor-neutral tiers `high-capability`/`general-purpose`/`fast`, with
  the same selection criteria, and added guidance to map these tiers to
  whatever models the host tool exposes.
- Rewrote all `Workflow`-script pseudocode examples (in
  `references/workflow-recipes.md` and `references/team-examples.md`)
  from literal JavaScript tied to the `Workflow` tool's API into
  generic, host-tool-neutral pseudocode.
- Dropped the upstream "v1 to v2 migration" section (`execution-modes.md`
  §5 in the original), which only concerned migrating between two prior
  versions of the Claude Code plugin, and replaced it with a short note
  on porting an existing tool-specific harness to this skill's portable
  primitives.
- Renamed the skills from `harness`/`evolve` to `agent-harness`/
  `agent-harness-evolve` to avoid colliding with the upstream Claude
  Code plugin's own `/plugin install harness` namespace.
- Added this NOTICE file and copied LICENSE verbatim, as required by
  the Apache License, Version 2.0.

All six team-architecture patterns, the quality-verification patterns
(adversarial verification, judge panels, loop-until-dry, multi-angle
sweeps, gap review), the QA-agent integration-coherence guidance, and
the skill-writing/testing guidance are preserved from the original work,
adapted only to remove tool-specific API calls.

See `skills/agent-harness/SKILL.md`'s "Attribution" section for a
pointer back to this file.
